    {
      "who": "DAD",
      "text": "Ha! I'm not sad, I promise. The onion has a sneaky trick.",
      "punch": "sneaky",
      "board": {
        "type": "big",
        "icon": "🧅",
        "text": "A sneaky onion trick",
        "cue": "trick"
      }
    },
    {
      "who": "LEO",
      "text": "What trick?"
    },
    {
      "who": "DAD",
      "text": "An onion is made of tiny bits called cells. When a grown-up cuts it, the cells break open.",
      "board": {
        "type": "big",
        "icon": "🧅",
        "text": "Cutting breaks the cells",
        "cue": "cells",
        "sub": "Only grown-ups cut!",
        "sub_cue": "grown"
      }
    },
    {
      "who": "DAD",
      "text": "Inside, two kinds of onion juice mix together and make an invisible gas that floats up into the air.",
      "board": {
        "type": "steps",
        "title": "The sneaky gas",
        "items": [
          {
            "icon": "🧪",
            "label": "Onion juices mix",
            "cue": "mix"
          },
          {
            "icon": "💨",
            "label": "They make a gas",
            "cue": "gas"
          },
          {
            "icon": "⬆️",
            "label": "It floats up",
            "cue": "floats"
          }
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "who": "LEO",
      "text": "And the gas goes in your eyes?"
    },
    {
      "who": "DAD",
      "text": "Yep! It stings a little. So your eyes make tears to wash it away.",
      "punch": "tears",
      "board": {
        "type": "big",
        "icon": "img:Human_physiology/Servier/tear-duct",
        "text": "Tears wash it away",
        "cue": "tears",
        "sub": "Eyes protect themselves",
        "sub_cue": "eyes"
      }
    },
    {
      "who": "LEO",
      "text": "Why would an onion do that?"
    },
    {
      "who": "DAD",
      "text": "Scientists think it's how onions protect themselves, so animals don't want to munch on them.",
      "board": {
        "type": "big",
        "icon": "🛡️",
        "text": "Onion protection!",
        "cue": "protect",
        "sub": "Scientists think",
        "sub_cue": "scientists"
      }
    },
    {
      "who": "LEO",
      "text": "Can we stop the tears?"
    },
    {
      "who": "DAD",
      "text": "One trick is to chill the onion in the fridge first. Cold onions let out less gas.",
      "board": {
        "type": "big",
        "icon": "❄️",
        "text": "Chill it first",
        "cue": "chill",
        "sub": "Less gas, fewer tears",
        "sub_cue": "less"
      }
    },
    {
      "who": "LEO",
      "text": "So cutting breaks the cells, the gas floats up, and my eyes wash it away!",
